{"resourceIdentifier":"2375","resourceName":"Jilin Sanchazi Afforestation Project","description":"Jilin Sanchazi Afforestation Project (herein after referred as “The project”) is located in Jiangyuan District, Jingyu County and Liuhe County, Baishang City, Jilin Province, China. The geographical coordinates of the project area are 126°18′27″~127°03′49″E, 42°04′39″~42°48′21″N. The project’s aim is to increase carbon sequestration and contribute to local sustainable development by planting trees on barren lands. The project proponent is Jilin Forest Industry Environmental Technology Co., Ltd.\r\n\r\nPrior to project activity, according to the baseline survey15, the project area has been barren since 1989, causing substantial soil and water erosion, biodiversity loss, contributing to climate change, perpetuated low income and living conditions in local communities. There are mainly scatter shrubs and grass land in the project area prior to the project activity.\r\n\r\nAn area of 22,564.64 ha, which belongs to Sanchazi Forestry Co., Ltd16, have been planted. All the trees are native species, including Korean pine, Spruce and Fraxinus mandshurica.\r\n\r\nThe implementation of the project would generate GHG emission removals and improve local environment by planting trees, enhance biodiversity conservation and climate change adaptation, improve soil and water conservation in project zone, strengthening the life skills of local communities and residents by providing them with relevant technical skills and training and create more permanent job opportunities for local women and increase income for local communities.\r\n\r\nThe project is estimated to generate GHG emission removals of 36,139,013tCO2e in 60 years, with an average annual GHG emission removal of 602,317tCO2e.","location":{"latitude":42.077500,"longitude":126.307499},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2022-04-15","endExclusive":"2022-05-16","endInclusive":"2022-05-15"},"at